# .loom/resync-ignore — paths Loom must not overwrite or delete on resync.
#
# See .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md for the full rule. Each entry below
# pins a deliberate, repo-specific divergence from the upstream rjwalters/loom
# defaults/ tree — guidance landed directly in this repo's installed copy
# because it is not (yet) upstreamed.
#
# Entries use the ".loom/"-relative report form: "commands/loom/judge.md",
# not ".claude/commands/loom/judge.md" (the latter would not match).

# #80 (commit 882f1cb): doctor.md and judge.md carry the merge-not-rebase
# warning for real-content conflicts (PR #73 re-decided a Judge's recorded
# merge-commit resolution via rebase and silently reintroduced a fixture
# cell collision), plus the rule to name which side of a real conflict was
# kept in the PR comment. rjwalters/loom's defaults/ has no equivalent, so
# resync-installed.sh's local-fix guard blocked both files and every
# scheduled fleet resync of this repo failed.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
commands/loom/doctor.md
commands/loom/judge.md
